{"kind":"report","text":"Source-only review complete at 10baa643ba4443427bc1aa5bf0d053bf36fef05a, tree299f7ccba8b6b59239469b6b51085aa04e657347, parent8e78. I read the primary note delta first, then the complete five-path diff and surrounding gateway, stream producer/relay and Node inventory code. Exactly five paths changed; all2771 other leaves retain the same mode/type/blob. No further mandatory Source finding identified within this repair; full native transfer acceptance remains open.\n\nThe gateway constructs a fresh transferred HTTP request from the admitted logical URL, original method/body, filtered headers and manual redirect. It carries HTTP message fields instead of inherited Request metadata. Descriptor equality, route/method admission, credential/cookie stripping, address-header forwarding, local header deadlines, disposal of late replies and response-body cancellation are unchanged. There is no tee, body buffering, additional request or retry. Remote caller AbortSignal propagation is not established or promised. I independently checked the exact pinned Request serializer: it attempts to serialize a present non-ignored signal and documents the unsupported signal type. [Pinned workerd Request serializer](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/cloudflare/workerd/v1.20260815.1/src/workerd/api/http.c%2B%2B). Cloudflare's current RPC contract specifies byte-oriented transferable streams and ownership transfer. [Cloudflare RPC stream contract](https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/runtime-apis/rpc/).\n\nThe outgoing relay adds only type:bytes to its stream constructor. Existing highWaterMark0, one upstream read per pull, error/end path, idempotent release and cancellation of the original reader remain byte-exact. Its actual unchanged producer allocates a fresh utf8 chunk for each head; no reused head buffer was found for byte enqueue to detach. The internal one-head queue and per-send session authorization are unchanged. I retain the runtime qualification on the